From 41f8b10049c280fdbf1f22dd3331e11c7fb73fe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:11:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(geometry): read OBJECTS of an AC1015 DXF as inert
 records

AC1015 exports put a group 102 reactor bracket in each object and write
LAYOUT, ACDBDICTIONARYWDFLT and ACDBPLACEHOLDER objects next to the
dictionaries. The reader refused the first bracket ("DICTIONARY:
unsupported dictionary group 102 or value") and every object type other
than DICTIONARY, so the real files did not import.

A balanced, non-nested 102 bracket is now opaque. A DICTIONARY keeps all
its field checks. Other objects are inert: the reader takes only the
handle and the owner from the common header and adds the object to the
ownership graph of #3176. Unowned objects, stray entities (AcDbEntity),
broken brackets and a missing ENDSEC stay named errors. The reader
keeps no OBJECTS data, so no object can change the imported geometry.

The real q04 export now gives the same 2 closed chains as its R12 twin.

Fixes #3450

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
